# Crayons React rules (dashboard, stateful sidebar, hybrid patterns)

## Imports

- Import wrappers from **`@freshworks/crayons/react`**:
  ```jsx
  import { FwButton, FwInput, FwSelect, FwTextarea, FwTabs, FwTab, FwToast, FwDataTable, FwSpinner, FwToggle } from '@freshworks/crayons/react';
  ```
- Import `defineCustomElements` from **`@freshworks/crayons/loader`** (not from `@freshworks/crayons`).

## Bootstrap (every entry that renders Crayons)

```jsx
import { defineCustomElements } from '@freshworks/crayons/loader';
import '@freshworks/crayons/css/crayons-min.css';
defineCustomElements();
```

- Call `defineCustomElements()` **exactly once per entry**, **before** `createRoot`.
- Import the CSS **exactly once per entry**.
- Do not call `defineCustomElements()` inside `useEffect` or any component body — it must run at module scope before rendering.

## Naming and props

- Component names are PascalCase with `Fw` prefix (`FwButton`, not `fw-button`).
- Custom-element attributes become camelCase props (`is-selectable` → `isSelectable`).
- DOM events become `on{EventName}` props (`fw-click` → `onFwClick`, `fw-change` → `onFwChange`).
- Event detail is on `event.detail` (typically `{ value }` or `{ checked }`).

## Forbidden patterns

- ❌ Mixing `<fw-button>` raw element with `<FwButton>` wrapper inside the same render tree.
- ❌ Loading the Crayons CDN script tag in HTML when also importing wrappers — pick one strategy. (This skill picks wrappers.)
- ❌ Setting `FwDataTable.columns`/`rows` as JSX props — they are **element properties**; assign via ref + `useEffect`:
  ```jsx
  const ref = useRef(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    if (ref.current) {
      ref.current.columns = COLUMNS;
      ref.current.rows = rows;
    }
  }, [rows]);
  return <FwDataTable ref={ref} label="…" />;
  ```
- ❌ Calling `toastRef.current.trigger()` before the toast component has mounted.

## Toast usage

```jsx
const toastRef = useRef(null);
// ...
<FwToast ref={toastRef} position="top-center" />
// trigger:
toastRef.current?.trigger({ type: 'success', content: 'Saved' });
```

Allowed `type` values: `success`, `error`, `warning`, `inprogress`.

## Tabs usage

```jsx
<FwTabs activeTabIndex={index} onFwChange={(e) => setIndex(e.detail.tabIndex)}>
  <FwTab tab-header="Overview">…</FwTab>
  <FwTab tab-header="Details">…</FwTab>
</FwTabs>
```

`tab-header` stays as a kebab-case JSX attribute string.

## CSS scope

`@freshworks/crayons/css/crayons-min.css` is global. Do not deep-style internals; if you need custom looks, use Crayons CSS variables (e.g. `--button-color`) on a wrapper class.
